                <pb facs="1215" n="1209" xml:id="pg1209"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                19, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In recent dispatches I have sent letters
                    between Hon. S. B. Dole, minister of foreign affairs, and myself in regard to my
                    “attitude showing the intention to use force.”</p>
                <p>I have the honor to transmit herewith the letters of Mr. Dole of January 11 and
                    18, 1894, and my reply of this and prior date, which will, on my part, end
                    correspondence on the subject.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis.</hi></signed></closer>






